@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Approvals and Gates in Azure Pipelines";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Ensure controlled and automated deployments using Approvals and Gates in Azure DevOps Pipelines.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What are Approvals and Gates?</h2>
        <p>
            Approvals and Gates are essential components in Azure Pipelines that help control and automate deployment workflows.
            They ensure that deployments meet predefined conditions before proceeding to the next stage.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/approvals-gates-overview.jpg" alt="Approvals and Gates Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Approvals and Gates enhance deployment governance and compliance.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Approvals in Azure Pipelines -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Approvals in Azure Pipelines</h2>
        <p>
            Approvals are manual checkpoints that require authorization before a deployment proceeds to the next stage. 
            They can be configured at various stages, ensuring that only authorized personnel can approve releases.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Pre-Deployment Approvals:</strong> Required before a stage begins.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Post-Deployment Approvals:</strong> Required after a stage completes successfully.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Multiple Approvers:</strong> Define one or more approvers for strict control.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Timeout and Auto-Reject:</strong> Set expiration limits for pending approvals.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/approvals.jpg" alt="Azure Pipelines Approvals" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Approvals ensure controlled releases within the CI/CD pipeline.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Gates in Azure Pipelines -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Gates in Azure Pipelines</h2>
        <p>
            Gates are automated policies that check predefined conditions before allowing a deployment to proceed. 
            They ensure compliance with business and security requirements.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Query Work Items:</strong> Ensure all work items linked to a release meet specific conditions.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Invoke REST API:</strong> Call external APIs to validate deployment readiness.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Check Azure Monitor Alerts:</strong> Validate system health before proceeding.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Evaluate Security Scans:</strong> Ensure no security vulnerabilities are present.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/gates.jpg" alt="Azure Pipelines Gates" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Gates provide automated validation for better deployment quality.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Configuring Approvals and Gates -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Configuring Approvals and Gates</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to configure Approvals and Gates in Azure Pipelines:</p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Navigate to Azure DevOps and open your Release Pipeline.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select the stage where you want to add Approvals and Gates.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on "Pre-deployment conditions" or "Post-deployment conditions".</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Enable "Approvals" and specify the approvers.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Enable "Gates" and define the required validation checks.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Save and trigger a new deployment to test the settings.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/configuring-approvals-gates.jpg" alt="Configuring Approvals and Gates" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Proper configuration ensures secure and compliant deployments.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Best Practices for Approvals and Gates</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Ensure only authorized users can approve releases.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate as Much as Possible:</strong> Use Gates to minimize manual interventions.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Regularly Review Approval Policies:</strong> Update approvers and security checks periodically.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor and Audit Deployments:</strong> Use logs and alerts to track approval and gate activities.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/best-practices-approvals-gates.jpg" alt="Best Practices for Approvals and Gates" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices improves deployment efficiency and security.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-dark">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Approvals and Gates in Azure Pipelines provide robust control over deployment workflows. 
            By implementing manual approvals and automated validation checks, teams can ensure quality, security, and compliance before moving software to production.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion-approvals-gates.jpg" alt="Approvals and Gates Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Effective use of Approvals and Gates enhances deployment governance.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
